── THE LIMIT, REPORTED EVERY RUN RATHER THAN DISCOVERED ──
This compares a picker against the CHECK IN sql/, which is the
repo's INTENDED constraint and not the live database's. A role
that is in the schema file and NOT YET MIGRATED is invisible here
-- that is the office_manager state as this is written. So:
  CAUGHT    a picker ahead of the schema file (drift)
  NOT CAUGHT a schema file ahead of production (lag)

